post_install() {
  cat <<'EOF'
Pi scans no system path by itself. Add the shared extension root once and
restart pi:

  ~/.pi/agent/settings.json
    "extensions": ["/usr/share/pi/extensions"]

That one directory entry loads every Pi extension installed by pacman, this
package included. On this machine the entry already exists, so a fresh
pacman -U needs only a pi restart: the provider registers as "opencode-zen"
and pi-bolt --list-models lists its models.

Other Pi extensions packaged by other maintainers install into the same root, so
one entry covers those too.

If your settings still name /usr/lib/pi/packages, replace that entry: the
extensions now install under /usr/share.
EOF
}
